From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:50:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Start a video after its fade from black, measured once

A video that comes in over its snapshot waited through its recording's
fade from black before the crossfade, 0.3 to 1 s more each time.

Each video's lead-in is now measured once, off the UI thread (ffmpeg's
first 1.5 s, at low priority), and kept by path, size and date in
memory and in videoleadin.cache. The video then starts at it
(":start-time"), so its first frame is lit and the crossfade starts at
once; a video not measured yet is measured first and waits for its light
as before. The cards shown and those loaded around them, and every
system's last played game, are measured ahead; nothing is measured
while a game runs.
